= Decision theory — Simple =

Decision theory is the study of choosing among alternatives. It separates the options available, what might happen after each option, how likely those outcomes are, and how the outcomes are valued. Some decision theory asks what a rational agent should choose; other work studies how people actually choose.

'''Important boundary:''' decision theory ≠ psychology of choice by definition.

